<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia, Belgium sign accord to protect investors.</title>
<headline>Tunisia, Belgium sign accord to protect investors.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisia and Belgium on Wednesday signed an accord to protect investments of their nationals in each of the two countries.</p>
<p>The accord was signed in Tunis by Belgian Foreign Affairs Minister Erik Derycke and his Tunisian counterpart Habib Ben Yahia.</p>
<p>Belgium is Tunisia's fourth partner in the number of investing firms and its fifth foreign trade partner.</p>
<p>Ben Yahia said 133 firms owned by Belgian private investors were operating in Tunisia. These firms were mainly in the textiles sector.</p>
</text>
